  "verbalization": "Sparfloxacin, a fluoroquinolone antibiotic, is linked to Abcc2 through a series of molecular and biological interactions. The evidence suggests that Sparfloxacin may act as a modulator of Abcc2, as it binds to the same target as Lomefloxacin, which itself binds to Abcc2. This indicates a potential shared mechanism of action between Sparfloxacin and Lomefloxacin in their interaction with Abcc2. The lowest common ancestor of Sparfloxacin and Lomefloxacin is positioned within the class of fluoroquinolones and quinolones, suggesting a broader pharmacological context. The presence of multiple pathways, including the resemblance of Sparfloxacin to Besifloxacin, further supports a common structural or functional relationship with quinolones, which in turn interact with Abcc2. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Sparfloxacin in influencing Abcc2 through quinolone-related mechanisms, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
